            <ArticleTitle>An 81-year-old man with an abnormal right-sided heart shadow on chest radiograph.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e52-e55</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0012-3692(15)30203-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1378/chest.14-1393</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 81-year-old man presented with a 1-week history of dry cough. He also complained of mild dyspnea, wheezing, and low-grade fever. He denied hemoptysis, fever, rashes, or chest pain. The patient's medical history included coronary artery bypass surgery, hypertension, gastroesophageal reflux disease, and COPD. The patient was a retired welder and an ex-smoker.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
